	<item>
		<title>
		By: Moses		</title>
		<link>https://nursesrevisionuganda.com/immunization/#comment-5747</link>

		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Moses]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sat, 30 Nov 2024 07:26:47 +0000</pubDate>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://nursesrevisionuganda.com/?p=3631#comment-5747</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[In reply to &lt;a href=&quot;https://nursesrevisionuganda.com/immunization/#comment-489&quot;&gt;Obore Joseph&lt;/a&gt;.

Polio is divided into two, OPV and IPV
so OPV is a live attenuated vaccine while IPV is inactivated polio vaccine. 
And both are given together at 14weeks.]]></description>
			<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>In reply to <a href="https://nursesrevisionuganda.com/immunization/#comment-489">Obore Joseph</a>.</p>
<p>Polio is divided into two, OPV and IPV<br />
so OPV is a live attenuated vaccine while IPV is inactivated polio vaccine.<br />
And both are given together at 14weeks.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
		
			</item>
